[74.74943, "o", "**Nothing in HANDOFF.md was actually unfinished — the ledger was stale, not blocked.**\r\n\r\nThe audit trail:\r\n\r\n- The one open entry, `2026-09-02 - Add search filtering`, had two unchecked steps and read \"Filtering exists; edge-case verification remains.\"\r\n- Commit `e5c6918` (\"Handle empty queries and the no-result case\") landed *after* the entry's own commit `4f25835`, and does exactly what the unchecked step described: `search.py:10-11` returns the full list for an empty query, the comprehension returns an empty list on no match, and `test_search.py` covers both cases.\r\n- I ran `python3 -m unittest test_search` rather than crediting the step from the diff alone: 3 tests, OK.\r\n\r\nSo the step was complete in code and only unrecorded in the ledger — the classic case of an old unchecked box that a later commit had already resolved.\r\n\r\nUpdates written (via the guard, against the version from the read):\r\n\r\n- The 2026-09-02 entry is now `Completed`, with each formerly-unchecked step annotated with the commit that"]
[74.750641, "o", " resolved it instead of being silently ticked or rewritten.\r\n- Added a `2026-09-07 - Audit the handoff ledger against current state` entry recording the evidence and the verification result, so the next agent can see why the boxes changed without this conversation.\r\n\r\nValidator passes; 2 structured tasks, both completed, no effective unfinished work in the ledger.\r\n\r\nTwo housekeeping notes: I didn't commit, since you didn't ask — `HANDOFF.md` is modified in the working tree. And the guard left a `HANDOFF.md.lock` artifact alongside the untracked `__pycache__/`; neither belongs in a commit if you make one.\r\n"]
[75.14115, "o", "\u001b[?25h"]
